+    "description": "On an affected kernel, a VPS process with access to a FUSE mount and its userspace filesystem server can race page transfer against request cancellation. The shared kernel may use request arguments after they have been freed. This could allow root access inside the VPS; a more advanced exploit could gain control of the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish either outcome on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel. Kernel warnings that may indicate this bug was triggered are monitored."
