+# CVE-2026-53388: FUSE splice request use-after-free
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-53388.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 7.8 (HIGH), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+fuse_try_move_folio unlocks the request but originally did not lock it again on successful page replacement. fuse_chan_abort can then finish the request and free fuse_io_args while subsequent copying still uses it. The stable correction locks the request before replacing the page-cache folio, preventing abort from freeing the arguments during the later copy. Older branches use the equivalent page helper.
+
+Mainline introduction: `2.6.35`, commit [`ce534fb052928ce556639d7ecf01cbf4e01321e1`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce534fb052928ce556639d7ecf01cbf4e01321e1). Mainline fixing commit: [`a078484921052d0badd827fcc2770b5cfc1d4120`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a078484921052d0badd827fcc2770b5cfc1d4120), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.95`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
