+# CVE-2026-63824: Asymmetric keyctl output-buffer overflow
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-63824.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 7.8 (HIGH), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+keyctl_pkey_params_get_2 sized an internal output buffer from the caller-provided short out_len, although the selected asymmetric cryptographic operation can emit its full primitive output. The fix sizes output from queried max_enc_size/max_dec_size/max_sig_size for the chosen operation. This is kernel heap overflow, not merely truncation of the user result.
+
+Mainline introduction: `4.20.0`, commit [`00d60fd3b93219ea854220f0fd264b86398cbc53`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00d60fd3b93219ea854220f0fd264b86398cbc53). Mainline fixing commit: [`cb481e59ea6cae3b7796ac1d7a22b6b24c3f3c0b`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb481e59ea6cae3b7796ac1d7a22b6b24c3f3c0b), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.95`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
