+# CVE-2026-63830: SK_MSG BPF scatterlist ownership corruption
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-63830.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 9.4 (CRITICAL), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+Scatterlist transforms moved SG entries without their sg.copy ownership bits. An externally backed entry such as a spliced file-page-cache page could then be exposed as writable SK_MSG ctx->data, allowing BPF stores to modify original page-cache bytes. The fix propagates/clears ownership through pull/push/pop/shift/xfer and TLS record splitting. The primitive is unauthorised backing-page modification, distinct from ordinary writable packet data.
+
+Mainline introduction: `4.20.0`, commit [`d3b18ad31f93d0b6bae105c679018a1ba7daa9ca`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3b18ad31f93d0b6bae105c679018a1ba7daa9ca). Mainline fixing commit: [`406e8a651a7b854c41fecd5117bb282b3a6c2c6b`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/406e8a651a7b854c41fecd5117bb282b3a6c2c6b), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.95`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
