+# CVE-2026-72069: PREEMPT_RT unlock RCU lifetime use-after-free
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-72069.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 9.8 (CRITICAL), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+The RT substitutes for spinlock/rwlock released their RCU read-side protection before the actual unlock had finished. A concurrent grace period could free the containing object while the unlock still accesses its lock, yielding a freed-object access/write. The fix moves rcu_read_unlock after the RT unlock operation, retaining migrate_enable ordering.
+
+Mainline introduction: `5.15.0`, commit [`0f383b6dc96e976dfbf2721b0bf10bd96103b341`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f383b6dc96e976dfbf2721b0bf10bd96103b341). Mainline fixing commit: [`89038cc87d80c77e7aa6f42a64b2573b74af339f`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89038cc87d80c77e7aa6f42a64b2573b74af339f), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.101`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
