+
+## Frozen evidence and reviewed lifecycle scope
+
+This dossier uses the single schema 8 snapshot collected at
+`2026-10-19T21:48:39Z`, SHA-256
+`61904e984266df2f6c53435b2b026b0d0980b35a23ed843eebf95b23c27c9274`.
+No per-CVE collection is performed. It contains 13 active nodes: 12 hypervisors
+report the fixed 6.12.113 source and one storage node lacks current/history
+security evidence. This is current-state evidence, not proof of earlier safety.
+The normal evaluator writes the tracked per-node conclusions; they are not
+edited manually.
+
+[Configuration commit e27882a9](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsfree-cz-configuration/commit/e27882a9bc8f6900903e6ae84841b9935190548c)
+first adds Node126 as a production hypervisor, including its node identity,
+module and cluster/netbootable registration. The independently reviewed parent
+`76055edbba3b3b4cf0cd6df45d2255e812d8aa6a` has neither that node nor its path.
+The frozen reconstructed history starts on the same day with booted release
+`6.12.70`, first observed at `2026-03-31T20:11:46Z`. Together these establish
+post-January lifecycle scope. The supported Node126-only history override starts
+at that retained baseline. The observation is not asserted as the exact
+production activation instant, and source/range/runtime classification still
+applies to every later interval. The global January 1 baseline is unchanged.
+There is no lifecycle override for storage161. Its reviewed operator-period
+exclusion below is separate from typed kernel-history evidence.
+
+Current runtime observations report `kernel.io_uring_disabled=0`,
+`kernel.io_uring_group=-1`, `kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled=0` and
+`kernel.perf_event_paranoid=2` on the 12 reporting hypervisors. Their exact collected
+configurations have `CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT=n`. These present facts do not reconstruct
+old config/LSM/program/device/CPU policy. The encrypted-key module is actually
+loaded on one reporting node, demonstrating why absence from a default preload
+list cannot establish fleet-wide non-exposure. Intel/AMD KVM vendor module
+observations do not by themselves prove nested VMX or IntelPT capabilities.
+
+## Operator-confirmed non-RT period
+
+On 2026-10-20 the operator was asked whether backuper2.prg ran without
+`CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT` throughout 2026-01-01 through 2026-10-19 and answered
+"1. yes". This direct period confirmation supersedes the initial current-only
+configuration observation and the unresolved historical storage conclusion.
+The API identity is Node161, `backuper2.prg`, role `storage`; the operator's
+`backuper2.prg.vpsfree.cz` command prompt names the same host. That initial
+confirmation was bounded to this node and assessment period. Later on
+2026-10-20 the operator clarified that RT has never been enabled anywhere on
+vpsFree.cz nodes. This broader operational statement supersedes the earlier
+uncertainty about whether other historical platform builds might have enabled
+RT. It does not supply missing historical build identities or configuration
+files.
+
+The preceding direct running-kernel observation corroborates the necessary
+configuration exclusion:
+
+```text
+[root@backuper2.prg.vpsfree.cz] zgrep -i preempt_rt /proc/config.gz
+# CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT is not set
+```
+
+The primary defect and fix require the substituted PREEMPT_RT implementation.
+Absence of VPS workloads alone would not exclude real host TCP/NFS/RCU locking
+paths. The operator's confirmation that RT mode was absent throughout the
+period supplies the positive negative-applicability fact for this dossier.
+The archived non-RT build is corroboration only and is not assigned to unknown
+historical storage boots.
+
+`platform.operator_node_exclusions["161"]` records this necessary-option
+exclusion for the exact API name and role, from `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z` through
+`2026-10-19T21:48:39Z`, inclusive. The upper timestamp is the frozen collection
+boundary within the confirmed October19 day. It is a claim-scope boundary, not
+a fabricated observation, deployment or mitigation time. The frozen storage
+record still lacks build/configuration/history data; those raw facts are not
+rewritten. The normal evaluator may classify this exact node as `not_affected`
+from the reviewed operator attestation when it covers the complete assessment
+interval and no exact retained configuration contradicts it. Missing raw option
+data does not contradict the statement. Another node, mismatched identity or
+collection outside the bound cannot inherit this exemption.
+
+Both affected roles, necessary CONFIG requirements, canonical upstream ranges,
+accepted mitigation lists and lifecycle override remain unchanged. No kernel
+build, historical event, mitigation date, raw configuration or manual per-node
+result is invented. The existing historical-attestation file and all consumed
+submission baselines remain untouched. Ordinary evaluation applies everywhere
+outside this bounded claim. A known conflicting exact configuration yields
+unknown rather than letting the operator statement override it.
+
+The matching tool/dossier revision is required to reproduce this new result.
+The exact consumed parent loader accepts the additive map, but its evaluator
+ignores it and conservatively retains storage unknown. The ordinary pre-write
+comparison must reject that old recalculation against the new resolved result;
+no digest or conclusion guard is weakened for rollback.
+
+The final platform applicability conclusion incorporates the later global
+operator confirmation: the necessary real-time mode was never enabled, so
+this vulnerability has not affected vpsFree.cz nodes. The existing bounded
+Node161 exclusion and version/history evaluation remain unchanged. Their
+twelve `mitigated` and one `not_affected` results retain their original reasons
+and dates; the version-derived mitigation intervals do not assert that RT was
+previously enabled or that actual exposure occurred. The redundant Node161
+public notes are removed. No per-build evidence or evaluation result is
+invented to encode the broader operational fact.
