+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-74517.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 9.3 (CRITICAL), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+Delayed I/O APIC EOI injection can try to deliver an IRQ to vCPUs after VM teardown has freed them. The fix cancels and flushes eoi_inject in kvm_arch_pre_destroy_vm, before vCPU destruction, while retaining VM interrupt-controller state until its normal destruction. Primary KASAN establishes an eight-byte stale vCPU access; it does not demonstrate host-root control.
+
+Mainline introduction: `6.14.0`, commit [`17bcd714426386fda741a4bccd96a2870179344b`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/17bcd714426386fda741a4bccd96a2870179344b). Mainline fixing commit: [`9910e835580fef3bef53b70241dd00c4bffad693`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9910e835580fef3bef53b70241dd00c4bffad693), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.105`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
