+# CVE-2026-74587 — SCTP cached ASCONF chunk use-after-free and second release
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+Peer restart invokes sctp_asconf_queue_teardown while the association stays alive. It freed the outbound ASCONF chunk without clearing addip_last_asconf. A delayed authenticated ASCONF_ACK can reuse that pointer and release the chunk again. The fix clears the cached pointer and consumes a stale T4 timer expiry when no outstanding ASCONF remains; stopping the timer alone does not wait for another CPU callback.
+
+The source establishes dangling-chunk use and a second release, plus the timer race addressed by the correction. CNA scenario impact is not a reproduced exploitation chain on this platform.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
