+# CVE-2026-74588 — SCTP stale chunk transport after retransmit-list move
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+__sctp_outq_flush_rtx moves a gap-acknowledged chunk to another transport transmitted list without updating chunk->transport. Peer ASCONF Delete-IP can free the old transport while the chunk resides on the new list and evades the old-list scrub. Later SACK reneging clears tsn_gap_acked and processing reaches tchunk->transport->flight_size -= sctp_data_size(tchunk) in the freed object. The fix rebinds chunk->transport at the list move.
+
+The upstream report supplies a KASAN UAF read, and the cited read-modify-write statement establishes a stale-object write target. This is stronger primitive evidence than the read-only first fault in 74586, but still not a complete reviewed node exploit.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.12**, commit [`1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`9f2cf069a9a72a2d6b97ca8b4c70e714aac99749`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=9f2cf069a9a72a2d6b97ca8b4c70e714aac99749). The 6.12 correction is [`e2e7c1de0e226ca1b7fea2de57a6c9bca408709b`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2e7c1de0e226ca1b7fea2de57a6c9bca408709b) in **6.12.104**.
