+    summary: "Kernel memory corruption"
+    description: >-
+      An IPv6 tunnel can reuse Home Address Option metadata from an outer ICMP packet when processing its quoted inner packet. A stale offset can then make an address swap corrupt kernel packet metadata. The tunnel support is built in, but the required Mobile IPv6 functionality is conditional on host module availability and matching tunnel and security state. If that path is available, exploitation could potentially support VPS-root or node compromise. The reviewed Linux record and fix do not establish a complete escape or access to another VPS. Invalid metadata can crash the shared kernel. Kernel warnings that may indicate this bug was triggered are monitored.
