+# CVE-2026-74597 — IPv6 tunnel ICMP stale Home Address Option metadata corruption
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+ip6ip6_err cloned an outer IPv6 ICMP error and pulled it to the quoted inner IPv6 packet without clearing skb->cb. Outer Home Address Option metadata dsthao then survived against the new packet origin. icmpv6_send calls mip6_addr_swap, whose stale offset can make HAO lookup/address swap run beyond the quote and corrupt skb_shared_info. The fix clears IP6CB on the clone before pulling/rebasing.
+
+The record/fix describe an out-of-bounds address swap corrupting shared skb metadata. They do not establish a full node exploit or arbitrary remote trigger independent of the MIP6 state requirements.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.22**, commit [`e490d1d85cf5e191791979e5f260d32eb4f703a8`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=e490d1d85cf5e191791979e5f260d32eb4f703a8), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`f803c086399da277b5d0ff36a107d0f162751800`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=f803c086399da277b5d0ff36a107d0f162751800). The 6.12 correction is [`484134e1eb07d700a73b1e4bbf3fb503e299be60`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/484134e1eb07d700a73b1e4bbf3fb503e299be60) in **6.12.104**.
+
