+| 6.18 | 6.18.0 | 6.18.45 | [4eb15c465337b18f44716c499cd6ad63eee0ad54](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4eb15c465337b18f44716c499cd6ad63eee0ad54) |
+| 7.1 | 7.1.0 | 7.1.9 | [fbf40faa0414b753212494ad197542002e66ed9e](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fbf40faa0414b753212494ad197542002e66ed9e) |
+
+Stable semantic-version entries, Git fix references and CPE applicability were checked together. The older LTS rows without a listed fix remain explicitly open-ended within the CNA global/CPE affected scope; their absence from the fix list is not evidence of safety. Branch-specific backport introductions, where listed, override the global mainline introduction. Other release families remain governed by the global boundary rather than an invented same-branch fix.
+
+The historical source gate was corrected during research: IPV6_TUNNEL is built in, while only MIP6 availability remains conditional. This is a reachability correction, not an ineffective upstream-fix exception. The first 6.12 correction remains6.12.104.
+
+## Tenant prerequisites and current downstream source
+
+Requires an IPv6-in-IPv6 tunnel ICMP error, outer Home Address Option accepted by the receive stack and malformed quoted destination-options geometry. Exact archived IPV6_TUNNEL=y means tunnel support is built in: an absent ip6_tunnel module is not protection. IPV6_MIP6=m compiles the HAO call sites under IS_ENABLED, but the valid HAO receive/XFRM path requires its MIP6 type registration/state. The mip6 module is not default preloaded and autoload defaults off. Thus actual host module availability is conditional; if available, namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN can configure suitable tunnel/XFRM state. A generic unrelated IPv6 packet is insufficient.
+
+The inspected vpsAdmin feature policy, generated LXC config, userns capability reset and default seccomp profile do not remove the cited namespace-scoped networking path. Full capabilities inside the container user namespace do not confer initial-user-namespace module-loading authority. Source defaults are not a measurement of a node or a tenant namespace. The explicit required interface options are `{"CONFIG_IPV6": "enabled", "CONFIG_IPV6_MIP6": "enabled", "CONFIG_IPV6_TUNNEL": "enabled"}`; an explicit disabled necessary interface can prove unreachability for that exact build. Compiled modules alone cannot prove actual load state.
+
+Current downstream Linux source reviewed at `1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa`:
+
+- [net/ipv6/ip6_tunnel.c](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/linux/blob/1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa/net/ipv6/ip6_tunnel.c)
+
