+# CVE-2026-74615 — VXLAN ageing timer on down device use-after-free
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+vxlan_changelink armed age_timer whenever the ageing interval changed, even for a never-up device. Device close skips ndo_stop for a down device, so vxlan_stop did not synchronously cancel that timer. free_netdev then freed the containing vxlan_dev. Timer expiry unlinks the queued entry before loading timer->function and writes through the freed list pointers. The fix requires netif_running before arming from changelink.
+
+The upstream report gives a KASAN eight-byte write in __run_timers and attributes the discovery to XBOW. The trace is a reproduced UAF primitive, not proof of a vpsAdminOS host exploit.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 8.8 (HIGH), `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **5.0.0**, commit [`40051c4dcad5b374156ad9cceae8d15c0ef1cb95`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=40051c4dcad5b374156ad9cceae8d15c0ef1cb95), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`b37971686ec59fb027fa4910ba16805e68fddb97`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=b37971686ec59fb027fa4910ba16805e68fddb97). The 6.12 correction is [`6b095e99b9e67ea31f0c4b00260e010898253519`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b095e99b9e67ea31f0c4b00260e010898253519) in **6.12.104**.
+
