+
+Stable semantic-version entries, Git fix references and CPE applicability were checked together. The older LTS rows without a listed fix remain explicitly open-ended within the CNA global/CPE affected scope; their absence from the fix list is not evidence of safety. Branch-specific backport introductions, where listed, override the global mainline introduction. Other release families remain governed by the global boundary rather than an invented same-branch fix.
+
+No correction exception changing this 6.12 fix boundary is established by the reviewed record and patch.
+
+## Tenant prerequisites and current downstream source
+
+Requires create/change/delete lifecycle of a VXLAN device that stays down and an ageing-interval change. Namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN is sufficient for these rtnetlink operations; no traffic, physical NIC or host privilege is needed. The module is explicitly preloaded in current OS policy, and CONFIG_VXLAN=m in the exact archived build. A tenant namespace administrator can reach this path; a new user+network namespace is another primary-described path when runtime policy permits creation.
+
+The inspected vpsAdmin feature policy, generated LXC config, userns capability reset and default seccomp profile do not remove the cited namespace-scoped networking path. Full capabilities inside the container user namespace do not confer initial-user-namespace module-loading authority. Source defaults are not a measurement of a node or a tenant namespace. The explicit required interface options are `{"CONFIG_VXLAN": "enabled"}`; an explicit disabled necessary interface can prove unreachability for that exact build. Compiled modules alone cannot prove actual load state.
+
+Current downstream Linux source reviewed at `1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa`:
+
+- [drivers/net/vxlan/vxlan_core.c](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/linux/blob/1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa/drivers/net/vxlan/vxlan_core.c)
+
+Platform sources used to bind the gates:
+
