+# CVE-2026-74616: XDP broadcast clone shared-info overlap
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-74616.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 9.8 (CRITICAL), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+xdpf_clone copied linear frame contents into one page and checked only PAGE_SIZE, omitting skb_shared_info tailroom. A larger original frame could fit that check yet overlap shared-info when converted back to skb; later writes corrupt XDP return metadata. The fix limits the clone to SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(PAGE_SIZE).
+
+Mainline introduction: `5.14.0`, commit [`e624d4ed4aa8cc3c69d1359b0aaea539203ed266`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e624d4ed4aa8cc3c69d1359b0aaea539203ed266). Mainline fixing commit: [`e48e8edbef2eb824201495daa5234560f632b23c`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e48e8edbef2eb824201495daa5234560f632b23c), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.104`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
