+# CVE-2026-74656 — IPv4 nexthop PMTU exception MTU-update use-after-free
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+fib_nhc_update_mtu walked nexthop exceptions under RTNL with rcu_dereference_protected(...,1), although PMTU exception removal uses fnhe_lock and RCU reclamation independently of RTNL. An entry can be unlinked and freed after a grace period while the walk retains its address. The correction adds the RCU read-side lifetime and takes fnhe_lock for each paired fnhe_pmtu/fnhe_mtu_locked update.
+
+The primary report supplies an eight-byte KASAN UAF read in the MTU-update walk. The same code also writes PMTU and lock fields. RCU alone would fix reclamation but not their paired-writer consistency; the reviewed correction addresses both. No complete exploit is supplied.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 7.8 (HIGH), `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
