@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# CVE-2026-74662 — IP fragment queue premature timer publication use-after-free
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+inet_frag_create armed a queue timer before inserting the queue into the fqdir rhashtable. Zero/negative namespace timeout can run expiry before publication; expiry marks complete, attempts to remove a node not yet inserted and drops the anticipated hash reference. Creation can then publish a completed queue without restoring that reference, leaving a stale hash node after the caller releases its reference. The fix publishes first and arms under the queue lock.
+
+The exact reference imbalance and dangling hash node are established by the primary record/patch. No complete privilege-escalation or host-execution exploit is supplied.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **4.17.0**, commit [`648700f76b03b7e8149d13cc2bdb3355035258a9`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=648700f76b03b7e8149d13cc2bdb3355035258a9), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`653d7ddf6cba867777a3d14c4f83ace008c5ad13`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=653d7ddf6cba867777a3d14c4f83ace008c5ad13). The 6.12 correction is [`39c6c4b267b65f00e0b0335a2ae00cbe9e3174f0`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39c6c4b267b65f00e0b0335a2ae00cbe9e3174f0) in **6.12.106**.
+
+| Branch | Affected from, inclusive | Fixed from, exclusive boundary | Corrective commit |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 4.4 | 4.4.174 | open-ended; no same-branch fix listed | not listed |
+| 4.19 | 4.19.0 | open-ended; no same-branch fix listed | not listed |
+| 5.4 | 5.4.0 | open-ended; no same-branch fix listed | not listed |
+| 5.10 | 5.10.0 | 5.10.267 | [f4e4dab62181b7fe7c011bed6fbef9fc3d48c769](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4e4dab62181b7fe7c011bed6fbef9fc3d48c769) |
+| 5.15 | 5.15.0 | 5.15.218 | [4ed0681dc2c1e0538b79d2fc56190ffcb369dacd](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ed0681dc2c1e0538b79d2fc56190ffcb369dacd) |
+| 6.1 | 6.1.0 | 6.1.185 | [08a04d7bfb9c103432561aff8a62b6872e694a6a](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08a04d7bfb9c103432561aff8a62b6872e694a6a) |
+| 6.6 | 6.6.0 | 6.6.154 | [d3ffb89b2944672cf7bdd8e9ee577d2043b4a956](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3ffb89b2944672cf7bdd8e9ee577d2043b4a956) |
+| 6.12 | 6.12.0 | 6.12.106 | [39c6c4b267b65f00e0b0335a2ae00cbe9e3174f0](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39c6c4b267b65f00e0b0335a2ae00cbe9e3174f0) |
+| 6.18 | 6.18.0 | 6.18.45 | [9f904dd3e455750e5d4ec9b2f134835811b85a2f](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9f904dd3e455750e5d4ec9b2f134835811b85a2f) |
+| 7.1 | 7.1.0 | 7.1.9 | [928128865e43b197e30688dc1bc991592c97edcf](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/928128865e43b197e30688dc1bc991592c97edcf) |
+
+Stable semantic-version entries, Git fix references and CPE applicability were checked together. The older LTS rows without a listed fix remain explicitly open-ended within the CNA global/CPE affected scope; their absence from the fix list is not evidence of safety. Branch-specific backport introductions, where listed, override the global mainline introduction. Other release families remain governed by the global boundary rather than an invented same-branch fix.
+
+The CNA lists an older 4.4.174 stable backport introduction before the mainline 4.17 introduction, with no same-branch fix. An explicit open-ended4.4 rule preserves that affected range. A positive source-default timeout is conditional trigger reduction, not a fleet/history non-exposure claim.
+
+## Tenant prerequisites and current downstream source
+
+Requires fragment queue creation and a namespace fragment timeout of zero or negative. The IPv4 ipfrag_time table points to net->ipv4.fqdir->timeout and is registered per network namespace. A tenant network administrator can change its namespace timeout and supply fragments; a host default30-second setting does not establish tenant state. INET fragment machinery is built and socket/network controls pass default seccomp.
+
+The inspected vpsAdmin feature policy, generated LXC config, userns capability reset and default seccomp profile do not remove the cited namespace-scoped networking path. Full capabilities inside the container user namespace do not confer initial-user-namespace module-loading authority. Source defaults are not a measurement of a node or a tenant namespace. The explicit required interface options are `{"CONFIG_INET": "enabled"}`; an explicit disabled necessary interface can prove unreachability for that exact build. Compiled modules alone cannot prove actual load state.
+
+Current downstream Linux source reviewed at `1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa`:
+
+- [net/ipv4/inet_fragment.c](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/linux/blob/1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa/net/ipv4/inet_fragment.c)
+
