+    summary: "Kernel memory corruption"
+    description: >-
+      AF_PACKET transmit rings can use inconsistent packet-header sizes when a VPS process with raw-packet and network-administration rights changes its network device concurrently. The resulting out-of-bounds write could let a process with those delegated rights gain root inside the VPS. A VPS administrator already has that access but could use the same shared-kernel corruption to attempt node compromise. The reviewed Linux record and fix do not establish a complete node escape or a specific route to another VPS. Failed attempts can crash the shared kernel. Kernel warnings that may indicate this bug was triggered are monitored.
+    response: >-
