+# CVE-2026-74668 — AF_PACKET TX_RING inconsistent header-length race
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+`tpacket_snd()` formerly read `dev->hard_header_len` separately for allocation, frame limits and construction in `tpacket_fill_skb()`. Concurrent device reconfiguration can leave too little reserved headroom or a negative copy length. The stable fix snapshots the length once and passes it through all these operations; the concrete primitive is an out-of-bounds packet-buffer write.
+
+The fix and CNA describe the size inconsistency and memory corruption. CNA scenario text infers privilege escalation from that primitive. This review did not reproduce a host exploit or establish controlled node execution.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 7.8 (HIGH), `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.31**, commit [`69e3c75f4d541a6eb151b3ef91f34033cb3ad6e1`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=69e3c75f4d541a6eb151b3ef91f34033cb3ad6e1), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`21b5953e7494c16a42e6cd8cf110e18d13ae4a6b`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=21b5953e7494c16a42e6cd8cf110e18d13ae4a6b). The 6.12 correction is [`016763e829cac37b3234eace86fd0a4c560de4a7`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/016763e829cac37b3234eace86fd0a4c560de4a7) in **6.12.104**.
+
