+# CVE-2026-74669 — IPVS tunnel ICMP stale IPv4 options stack overwrite
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+ip_vs_in_icmp rebases an skb from the outer ICMP packet to the quoted original request before icmp_send, but IPCB(skb)->opt still described the outer header. A timestamp-option offset can then address the quoted transport bytes. __ip_options_echo interprets one such byte as length and copies into fixed-size option storage on the __icmp_send stack. The fix zeroes only the stale option metadata after the network-header reset, preserving the ingress interface.
+
+The source specifies a kernel stack out-of-bounds copy and its stale-offset origin. It does not establish a complete bypass of stack/control-flow protections or a working node exploit.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **3.7.0**, commit [`f2edb9f7706dcb2c0d9a362b2ba849efe3a97f5e`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=f2edb9f7706dcb2c0d9a362b2ba849efe3a97f5e), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`e0ba936287dfe9783426aac27e5fd76fe35b38c9`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=e0ba936287dfe9783426aac27e5fd76fe35b38c9). The 6.12 correction is [`6f46fc460e9316062bdcdf89199eb5d7a33da33b`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f46fc460e9316062bdcdf89199eb5d7a33da33b) in **6.12.104**.
+
