+# CVE-2026-74688 — SCTP queued control-chunk transport use-after-free
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+sctp_make_heartbeat_ack caches a destination transport without taking a reference. With src_out_of_asoc_ok the reply stays on control_chunk_list. Peer removal previously scrubbed only out_chunk_list, leaving the control reply dangling. ASCONF_ACK later clears suppression and transmission dereferences the freed transport. The fix also clears matching transport pointers in control_chunk_list.
+
+The reviewed report/fix establish stale transport use. They do not supply a complete controlled-write or privilege-escalation chain; CNA Critical impact remains attributed separately.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
