+# CVE-2026-74724 — IPVS ICMP NAT mutable IPv4 header out-of-bounds write
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+ip_vs_nat_icmp re-read the embedded IPv4 ihl after validating the header. A local packet producer able to change the shared packet concurrently can alter this length and make the NAT transport-port write address bytes outside the validated range. The fix passes the previously parsed ciph descriptor, uses ciph->len for the transport offset and snapshots related IPv4 header checks.
+
+The primary report identifies a concrete out-of-bounds write after a mutable header check, not a complete exploit. The CVSS local-attacker inference is preserved separately.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 7.8 (HIGH), `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.12**, commit [`1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`646922a0379496154e8c8faca4f8e2fd9100cacc`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=646922a0379496154e8c8faca4f8e2fd9100cacc). The 6.12 correction is [`be65fa324640c7a95e30b146159a2be5cc73f22e`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be65fa324640c7a95e30b146159a2be5cc73f22e) in **6.12.104**.
+
