+| 6.18 | 6.18.0 | 6.18.46 | [d9d3050a70efe217e73a0751e55fdae6a7092620](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9d3050a70efe217e73a0751e55fdae6a7092620) |
+| 7.1 | 7.1.0 | 7.1.10 | [d16b71231e65cb05daea2b45701fcf09cef041e7](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d16b71231e65cb05daea2b45701fcf09cef041e7) |
+
+Stable semantic-version entries, Git fix references and CPE applicability were checked together. The older LTS rows without a listed fix remain explicitly open-ended within the CNA global/CPE affected scope; their absence from the fix list is not evidence of safety. Branch-specific backport introductions, where listed, override the global mainline introduction. Other release families remain governed by the global boundary rather than an invented same-branch fix.
+
+No correction exception changing this 6.12 fix boundary is established by the reviewed record and patch.
+
+## Tenant prerequisites and current downstream source
+
+Requires registered flowtable functionality, configured flow offload and insertion concurrent with GC. Exact archived CONFIG_NF_FLOW_TABLE=m and NFT_FLOW_OFFLOAD=m do not prove availability. Current OS policy does not preload these modules and disables autoload, so this requires host/operator module activation or another evidenced availability path before a namespace administrator can configure the flowtable. It is not an ordinary tenant feature toggle under inspected defaults. Missing runtime module/history evidence is not a proven exclusion.
+
+The inspected vpsAdmin feature policy, generated LXC config, userns capability reset and default seccomp profile do not remove the cited namespace-scoped networking path. Full capabilities inside the container user namespace do not confer initial-user-namespace module-loading authority. Source defaults are not a measurement of a node or a tenant namespace. The explicit required interface options are `{"CONFIG_NF_FLOW_TABLE": "enabled"}`; an explicit disabled necessary interface can prove unreachability for that exact build. Compiled modules alone cannot prove actual load state.
+
+Current downstream Linux source reviewed at `1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa`:
+
+- [net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/linux/blob/1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c)
+
+Platform sources used to bind the gates:
+
+- [vpsAdmin feature defaults](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadmin/blob/fb2f51222503a45f2e5a42af505f719e44279ed0/api/models/vps_feature.rb)
+- [Container identity and security-profile generation](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/osctld/templates/ct/config.erb), [common/userns includes](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/osctld/configs/lxc/common.conf)
+- [Pinned LXC user-namespace capabilities](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/lxc/blob/267e7844c122b9be56ca8a1ccc3d2f4d8986c326/config/templates/userns.conf.in), [default syscall filter](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/lxc/blob/267e7844c122b9be56ca8a1ccc3d2f4d8986c326/config/templates/common.seccomp)
+- [Module preload/autoload policy](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/os/modules/config/kernel.nix), [kernel tunables](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/os/modules/config/tunables.nix)
+- [Kernel build policy](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/os/packages/linux/common-config.nix), [frozen 6.12.95 recipe](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/c065fa2f8485399737e20e8ef9e44299d0766654/os/packages/linux/boot-6.12.95.nix)
+- [Canonical historical livepatch coverage](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/docs/os/livepatches/6.12.95.md)
+
+## Impact and protections
+
+If the conditional module/configuration path is available, UAF writes could potentially support VPS-root or node-root compromise. The reviewed record/fix does not establish a complete execution chain or access to another VPS. Failed accesses can fault the shared kernel. Source defaults narrow expected exposure but cannot prove every production node/history was safe.
+
+The archived 6.12.95 build enables allocator randomization/freelist hardening, zeroing on allocation/free and FORTIFY. It lacks HARDENED_USERCOPY. These are source/configuration facts for that archived build, not universal fleet facts. They can change reuse opportunities or catch some bounds violations, but do not repair the missing lifetime/reference or inconsistent-size operation. They do not establish that this exact primitive is prevented. Default seccomp does not filter the networking operations used here; initial-userns module-loading restrictions do not undo an already available interface. Runtime LSM/profile overrides require the shared typed evidence and further source qualification when relevant. Kernel warning monitoring can detect failed triggers; it is not prevention and does not establish whether production exploitation occurred.
+
+## Role, history and mitigation contract
+
+Only role `node` is included because the assessed path uses VPS-controlled sockets, network namespaces or tenant device/configuration lifecycle. Storage nodes do not run VPS workloads. A separately established real host-service use would need its own scope review; old release age alone is not sufficient to add storage.
+
+The required history begins `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z` as a review window, not an asserted introduction or deployment date. Only the independently reviewed Node126 lifecycle override described below is used; no historical attestation or old dossier override is inferred or copied. A current fixed release does not prove earlier safety; affected historical stable releases with missing configuration are conservatively affected after this reachability review. Missing baseline/transition evidence remains unknown under the existing evaluator.
+
+Module availability and flowtable/rule state are the material prerequisites. The autoload source default is not encoded as a safe sysctl predicate: it neither unloads already registered modules nor establishes all historical load states.
+
+Runtime module/type registration and tenant protocol/device state are not generic schema predicates. They remain explicit prerequisites rather than ignored YAML keys or manual per-node status edits. Accepted-build and eBPF exceptions remain empty. Livepatch exceptions, if any, are qualified by the exact content and identity review recorded in this analysis; an empty list does not assert historical absence. The canonical coverage page alone proves neither activation nor a safe deployment. Quarantined livepatch v6 is not recommended for application, while independently source-correct, observed enabled/stable historical protection must still be preserved. Actual mitigation times and observation-state conclusions come from the normal evaluator against the frozen shared snapshot, not from this source paragraph.
+
+## Reproducible source receipts and remaining evidence
+
+- [Primary CVE record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-74746.json); [CVE record view](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-74746). CNA snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`; retained record SHA-256 `f5b63b0c82cd598cef48f069b1da18c01e8dd15958e72ef9f77ff2b07d52afe9`.
+- [Exact stable fix](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/972fdf7c4f5c282a239c88fea614b056c33dc025); retained patch SHA-256 `5d08d302b9403ecec66e5310a4483c147a0bc7d7540268c10f77cbfd4024d780`. Missing local partial-clone objects were read only via exact stable-maintainer mirror HTTP patches, never by repository fetch.
+- Current Linux source snapshots and hashes are retained in the session's `assessment/implementer1/source-manifest.json`; exact fix access methods/URLs/hashes in `fix-source-manifest.json`.
+- Archived configuration SHA-256 `c10922b492fdf39ed3027b9c8f7ce2846a5d3799d57d417a161595fa81a64969`, Linux `a2384967b90f24d2470c9eb15f0e66d938df7e08`; scope is the archived build, not fleet history.
+- The frozen typed snapshot was evaluated using the existing CLI, with no API call or recollection. Exact booted/current identities, configuration catalogs, role and transitions are retained in the ignored evidence and tracked evaluation. No exploit test, kernel build or remote draft write was performed by this owner.
+
+## Frozen evaluation review
+
+The existing CLI evaluated all 13 active nodes against schema8 snapshot collected 2026-10-19T21:48:39Z, byte SHA-256 `61904e984266df2f6c53435b2b026b0d0980b35a23ed843eebf95b23c27c9274`. The first evaluation retained one unknown because its history and reconstruction began after January. Architect subsequently independently reviewed configuration commit `e27882a9bc8f6900903e6ae84841b9935190548c`, its parent `76055edbba3b3b4cf0cd6df45d2255e812d8aa6a`, and the frozen initial boot. The commit first adds Node126 as a production hypervisor and its reconstructed boot begins the same day. This dossier uses the supported Node126-only `history_start_overrides` value `2026-03-31T20:11:46Z`, citing that commit. The value is the first retained baseline, not an asserted exact production deployment instant; the source commit itself predates that observation. Global January scope remains unchanged and ordinary affected/fixed/mitigation classification still applies throughout the scoped history. No storage override is applied. The final result and completeness are retained in `evaluation.json`. The excluded storage row lacks current timestamps, so its evidence is not certified fresh; the conclusion comes only from the tenant-only role scope, not a kernel-safety finding for a real storage workload.
+
+No current configuration/catalog/sysctl unknown arose in this dossier. Module/type/tenant-network prerequisites remain analyst qualifications where unmodeled; historical missing configuration is not converted into proof of safety. This is an unpublished assessment result, not publication readiness. Exact per-node reasons and times remain in `evaluation.json`.
