+# CVE-2026-74753: perf EXIT group-leader use-after-free
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-74753.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 7.8 (HIGH), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+remove_on_exec detaches a perf group and puts its leader in EXIT, while its descriptor can stay open. Accepting a new sibling under that detached leader leaves a stale group_leader pointer when the leader closes because the attach bit is already clear. The fix rejects EXIT leaders both early and under the shared context mutex. The earlier detach-on-exec correction introduced this regression; .95 predates the6.12.96 introduction.
+
+Mainline introduction: `7.2.0-rc1`, commit [`037a3c43edfb597665dd34457cd22b14692f2ba3`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/037a3c43edfb597665dd34457cd22b14692f2ba3). Mainline fixing commit: [`fa091f46c3833fb22384f10eade2b4e1e1d0b278`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fa091f46c3833fb22384f10eade2b4e1e1d0b278), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.108`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
+| Branch | Affected from (inclusive) | Fixed from (exclusive affected bound) | Introduction commit | Fix commit |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 6.6 | 6.6.145 | 6.6.156 | [`4cdb1b3ab96e`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cdb1b3ab96eb1b7eb70bc5c82fede334bd60df2) | [`ce12e1170c0c`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce12e1170c0c78dffb9b28af6d287492ae7dd99d) |
+| 6.12 | 6.12.96 | 6.12.108 | [`39358e856fb8`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39358e856fb89e62e3c8d7389a2dc4ec33dbe90e) | [`e593031ff19a`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e593031ff19a9484e8a00bc47edd447187721846) |
+| 6.18 | 6.18.39 | 6.18.46 | [`a2d5d3ee7b6e`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2d5d3ee7b6e3953114726b1521e62123ab5b043) | [`7a03413f31c1`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a03413f31c196ab3894f988cdce0bb47b4fec42) |
+| 7.1 | 7.1.4 | 7.1.10 | [`06ccef0434e9`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06ccef0434e98058ddae7bcebc901f93d22b7653) | [`7ce010275c53`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ce010275c531475f9d6e7efb11b9e522c74ed2e) |
+
+Branches with direct CNA stable fixes and explicit older backport introductions are represented separately. Open EOL long-term branches inherit the original introduced code: after checking the CNA commit/CPE scope, no same-branch fix is asserted without a cited correction. Other short-lived branches use the stated global bounds; a custom source build needs an exact source identity rather than release-number inference. Makefile versions at individual fix commits precede the stable release bump and are used to identify branch, not to invent the first containing release.
+
+## Tenant reachability and configuration
+
+CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS=y in the exact archived build. kernel.perf_event_paranoid=2 prohibits unprivileged kernel tracing and CPU-wide events but permits a process own per-task userspace event with exclude_kernel and appropriate sample flags. A software event is sufficient for the group lifecycle; no IntelPT hardware is needed for this CVE. Default seccomp permits perf_event_open; LSM restrictions remain runtime policy.
+
+The inspected current vpsAdmin feature/device code, vpsAdminOS container template and selected LXC profiles establish source behavior only. The template includes UID/GID mappings and the userns profile; capabilities retained there belong to the tenant user namespace. They do not satisfy an initial-user-namespace capability check. The default seccomp denylist blocks module loading and selected host interfaces, not arbitrary Linux syscalls; a per-container override remains a runtime fact.
+
+Necessary vulnerable-interface options declared for the shared collector:
+- `CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS`: archived .95 value `y`; requirement `enabled`.
+
+Archived exact .95 configuration SHA-256 is `c10922b492fdf39ed3027b9c8f7ce2846a5d3799d57d417a161595fa81a64969`, extracted from the frozen build NAR whose decompressed SHA-256 is `1b8ee65eed800b9ad10219936c50aa9b62fdae4f78ff9adcfaf2051eec40c229`. Producing vpsAdminOS revision is `c065fa2f8485399737e20e8ef9e44299d0766654`, Linux `a2384967b90f24d2470c9eb15f0e66d938df7e08`. This supports only that archived build, not every node or historical interval.
+
+Current downstream source check: Current .113 perf_event_open rejects group_leader->state<=PERF_EVENT_STATE_EXIT before and after taking the context mutex, matching e593031f. Mainline introduction037a3c43 has Makefile7.2.0-rc1 and correctionfa091f46 precedes final7.2. The exact global interval is rc1..final, while stable ranges are explicitly .96–.107 on6.12. The existing evaluator strips release-candidate suffixes: actual7.2 RC/custom releases must be flagged by the shared snapshot gate and escalated, never hand-classified or replaced with an invented released mainline interval.
+
