+# CVE-2026-80521: AF_UNIX garbage-collector SCC use-after-free
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-80521.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 7.8 (HIGH), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+An SCM_RIGHTS send can publish a graph edge before its skb is queued. Concurrent closes let garbage collection partly free a strongly connected component while a surviving vertex retains scc_entry pointing at a freed vertex. The next fast SCC walk follows that stale link. The fix unlinks scc_entry when unix_del_edge removes the final outgoing edge. List traversal/collection through reclaimed vertices supplies a plausible corruption primitive, not a platform exploit demonstration.
+
+Mainline introduction: `6.10.0`, commit [`4090fa373f0e763c43610853d2774b5979915959`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4090fa373f0e763c43610853d2774b5979915959). Mainline fixing commit: [`594d905195024b228c962627ae5ae7c17bd582a4`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/594d905195024b228c962627ae5ae7c17bd582a4), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.111`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
