+## Platform prerequisites, exact source and roles
+
+MPTCP is absent from the exact archived .95 build (CONFIG_MPTCP=n); tenant sysctls cannot enable compiled-out code. The negative conclusion applies to that exact build only. A kernel with MPTCP enabled additionally needs MPTCP sockets and negotiated protocol state; Fast Open defect80585 needs a listening endpoint, server Fast Open and valid cookie. Host net.mptcp.enabled or net.ipv4.tcp_fastopen cannot prove the tenant network namespace setting; namespace network administration can configure its own settings. Storage backup/NFS workload does not establish MPTCP sockets, so role node only under this tenant assessment. Actual kernels/history require the shared snapshot.
