+# CVE-2026-80714 — IPVS synchronized one-packet connection stale hash entry
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+A synchronized IPVS connection may be imported before its destination exists. Later ip_vs_bind_dest copied ONE_PACKET from the added destination into an already-hashed connection. Expiry then skipped unlinking conn_tab and freed the object, leaving stale hash nodes. The fix strips IP_VS_CONN_F_ONE_PACKET when binding a synchronized connection.
+
+The primary fix establishes dangling connection hash nodes with subsequent UAF potential. It does not supply a complete kernel-execution exploit.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.36**, commit [`26ec037f9841e49cc5c615deb8e1e73e5beab2ca`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=26ec037f9841e49cc5c615deb8e1e73e5beab2ca), and the mainline fix at **7.2.0**, commit [`a63d2dbaeb50a85d4c976b15a36e6b0c7113db5b`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=a63d2dbaeb50a85d4c976b15a36e6b0c7113db5b). The 6.12 correction is [`4649e6faeecdc2d44bfa6ccbe405eef27e55d816`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4649e6faeecdc2d44bfa6ccbe405eef27e55d816) in **6.12.103**.
+
