+
+Stable semantic-version entries, Git fix references and CPE applicability were checked together. The older LTS rows without a listed fix remain explicitly open-ended within the CNA global/CPE affected scope; their absence from the fix list is not evidence of safety. Branch-specific backport introductions, where listed, override the global mainline introduction. Other release families remain governed by the global boundary rather than an invented same-branch fix.
+
+No correction exception changing this 6.12 fix boundary is established by the reviewed record and patch.
+
+## Tenant prerequisites and current downstream source
+
+Requires IPVS backup synchronization in the namespace, imported connection before its destination, later destination binding with ONE_PACKET (UDP in current code), and expiry/lookup activity. IPVS is preloaded. Current namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN permits IPVS service and synchronization control; the peer/sync network must be arranged. Ordinary unrelated traffic on an unconfigured namespace is insufficient. No initial-userns capability or special hardware is identified.
+
+The inspected vpsAdmin feature policy, generated LXC config, userns capability reset and default seccomp profile do not remove the cited namespace-scoped networking path. Full capabilities inside the container user namespace do not confer initial-user-namespace module-loading authority. Source defaults are not a measurement of a node or a tenant namespace. The explicit required interface options are `{"CONFIG_IP_VS": "enabled"}`; an explicit disabled necessary interface can prove unreachability for that exact build. Compiled modules alone cannot prove actual load state.
+
+Current downstream Linux source reviewed at `1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa`:
+
+- [net/netfilter/ipvs/ip_vs_conn.c](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/linux/blob/1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa/net/netfilter/ipvs/ip_vs_conn.c)
+
+Platform sources used to bind the gates:
+
