+# CVE-2026-80725 — BIG TCP GRO IPv6 jumbo-header out-of-bounds write
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+skb_gro_receive allowed aggregation past64KiB using skb_headroom rather than actual bytes before the MAC header. For IPv6 with mac_header<8, later temporary HBH jumbo-header insertion memmoves before skb->head and wraps mac_header. The old criteria also admitted non-IP or encapsulated flows. The stable correction requires plain IPv4/IPv6 TCP, no encapsulation and actual IPv6 MAC-header room; unsuitable flows flush at the legacy size.
+
+The primary record identifies a concrete out-of-bounds memmove and geometry constraint. It does not supply a complete exploit on the container platform.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **5.19.0**, commit [`0fe79f28bfaf73b66b7b1562d2468f94aa03bd12`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=0fe79f28bfaf73b66b7b1562d2468f94aa03bd12), and the mainline fix at **7.0.0**, commit [`81be30c1f5f2bffda1f04c0efd0746af10b9643a`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=81be30c1f5f2bffda1f04c0efd0746af10b9643a). The 6.12 correction is [`03cb8cc2961f5f781d12e903782cb3815ed84b1c`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03cb8cc2961f5f781d12e903782cb3815ed84b1c) in **6.12.106**.
+
+| Branch | Affected from, inclusive | Fixed from, exclusive boundary | Corrective commit |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 6.1 | 6.1.0 | 6.1.185 | [37a5dcd6837fc2afc44a7bc3ed8af4e983783d46](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37a5dcd6837fc2afc44a7bc3ed8af4e983783d46) |
+| 6.6 | 6.6.0 | 6.6.154 | [e907bf694ed55bdfe421be99dba35751a655df25](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e907bf694ed55bdfe421be99dba35751a655df25) |
+| 6.12 | 6.12.0 | 6.12.106 | [03cb8cc2961f5f781d12e903782cb3815ed84b1c](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03cb8cc2961f5f781d12e903782cb3815ed84b1c) |
+| 6.18 | 6.18.0 | 6.18.47 | [3ce832e2bd431d0c12ba525ed73ad8fbc4191da5](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ce832e2bd431d0c12ba525ed73ad8fbc4191da5) |
+
+Stable semantic-version entries, Git fix references and CPE applicability were checked together. The older LTS rows without a listed fix remain explicitly open-ended within the CNA global/CPE affected scope; their absence from the fix list is not evidence of safety. Branch-specific backport introductions, where listed, override the global mainline introduction. Other release families remain governed by the global boundary rather than an invented same-branch fix.
+
+Mainline 7.0+ is fixed by the different rewrite81be30c1f5f2 (dropping HBH for BIG TCP RX), while older stable branches require this separate correction. The explicit6.12 rule remains affected until6.12.106; the mainline7.0 boundary must not be interpreted as a same-branch6.12 fix. The primary Fixes trailers mention both initial BIG TCP0fe79f28bfaf and later IPv4 relaxationb1a78b9b9886; the CNA global introduction5.19 is retained.
+
+## Tenant prerequisites and current downstream source
+
+Requires GRO/BIG TCP aggregation beyond64KiB on a participating device and crafted packet geometry. Tenant network administrators can change IFLA_GRO_MAX_SIZE through namespace-scoped rtnetlink; AF_PACKET injection additionally requires CAP_NET_RAW. The default syscall profile permits these operations and af_packet is preloaded. Ordinary traffic at the legacy aggregation limit does not establish the write. No physical NIC offload is a mandatory source gate for the described software-GRO path.
+
+The inspected vpsAdmin feature policy, generated LXC config, userns capability reset and default seccomp profile do not remove the cited namespace-scoped networking path. Full capabilities inside the container user namespace do not confer initial-user-namespace module-loading authority. Source defaults are not a measurement of a node or a tenant namespace. The explicit required interface options are `{"CONFIG_IPV6": "enabled"}`; an explicit disabled necessary interface can prove unreachability for that exact build. Compiled modules alone cannot prove actual load state.
+
+Current downstream Linux source reviewed at `1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa`:
+
+- [net/core/gro.c](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/linux/blob/1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa/net/core/gro.c)
+
