+# CVE-2026-80841 — AF_PACKET vmalloc TX_RING mapping use-after-free
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+Transmit skbs retain ring-frame pointers. Page references preserve page-backed blocks, but not a vmalloc virtual mapping. Ring replacement or socket closure could unmap vmalloc storage while late completion still writes a timestamp/status. The fix orders pending decrements after frame stores, rechecks replacement under pg_vec_lock, and defers vmalloc vector destruction until sk_wmem_alloc accounting shows the skbs finished; pending_refcnt lives until final socket destruction.
+
+The reviewed source establishes late stores through an expired mapping, rather than merely a retained page reference. No complete code-execution chain or platform escape is supplied by this review.
+
+No formal CVSS metric is supplied in the reviewed Linux CNA container. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
