+
+The inspected .113 source contains later AF_PACKET changes as well. In particular the subsequent CVE-2026-98503 fix must not be confused with this lifetime correction or used to move its first fixed boundary away from 6.12.111.
+
+## Tenant prerequisites and current downstream source
+
+The socket creation gate is namespace-scoped CAP_NET_RAW in packet_create(). A tenant process with that right can allocate a TX_RING, submit traffic and close/replace its ring. The vulnerable lifetime additionally requires a vmalloc-backed allocation and outstanding transmit completion; not every ring uses vmalloc. CONFIG_PACKET is enabled and af_packet is explicitly preloaded in the inspected OS source. Network administration may help arrange completion timing but is not the socket creation check.
+
+The inspected vpsAdmin feature policy, generated LXC config, userns capability reset and default seccomp profile do not remove the cited namespace-scoped networking path. Full capabilities inside the container user namespace do not confer initial-user-namespace module-loading authority. Source defaults are not a measurement of a node or a tenant namespace. The explicit required interface options are `{"CONFIG_PACKET": "enabled"}`; an explicit disabled necessary interface can prove unreachability for that exact build. Compiled modules alone cannot prove actual load state.
+
+Current downstream Linux source reviewed at `1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa`:
+
+- [net/packet/af_packet.c](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/linux/blob/1dfea587406b7dd79973831d1677fb2418e5e9aa/net/packet/af_packet.c)
+
