+    summary: "Kernel memory corruption"
+    description: >-
+      An SCTP DATA packet can restore a removed transport into the association state while authenticated address reconfiguration is taking place. A later acknowledgement then reads freed kernel memory. A VPS administrator can enable the required protocol features. The reviewed Linux record and fix do not establish a complete path to VPS root, node control or another VPS from this stale read. The invalid access can crash the shared kernel and interrupt other tenants. Kernel warnings that may indicate this bug was triggered are monitored.
+    response: >-
