+# CVE-2026-89478 — SCTP removed transport restored by queued DATA chunk
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+A packet lookup or backlog reference keeps a transport alive while authenticated ASCONF DEL-IP removes it from the association. A later DATA chunk can put that dead transport back into last_data_from. When the temporary reference ends, RCU frees it and a delayed SACK carries the stale pointer to sctp_outq_select_transport. The fix drops chunks whose transport is dead under the association socket lock in sctp_inq_push.
+
+The specific primary consequence is a freed transport state read; broader CNA confidentiality/integrity claims are inference. A complete host exploit is not established by this source review.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.12**, commit [`1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2), and the mainline fix at **7.3.0**, commit [`03a9d10ecf71f54b2af8020935f2033d4a132be5`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=03a9d10ecf71f54b2af8020935f2033d4a132be5). The 6.12 correction is [`c6c86a5e62a4fec36692ddd64b9144b660f71f96`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6c86a5e62a4fec36692ddd64b9144b660f71f96) in **6.12.109**.
+
