+# CVE-2026-89479 — SCTP endpoint packet processing after association deletion
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+A bundled COOKIE ECHO/SHUTDOWN/SHUTDOWN_ACK packet can create, cache and delete its association before the endpoint loop reaches another chunk. There is no held association reference. In task-context socket-backlog processing, the next chunk writes last_time_heard through the freed transport and enters sctp_do_sm with the freed association. The fix marks the packet for discard before deleting its own association, while preserving temporary duplicate-cookie deletion semantics.
+
+The source gives both a stale transport write and continued state-machine use, not merely a NULL crash. Reliable kernel execution is not demonstrated by this review.
+
+Linux CNA cvssV3_1: 9.8 (CRITICAL), `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.12**, commit [`1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2), and the mainline fix at **7.3.0**, commit [`47e15a8d12e366d0d261bcbc394394f44418938d`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=47e15a8d12e366d0d261bcbc394394f44418938d). The 6.12 correction is [`ee3f04cf566f6041aa9a0360494fd8db5ade383a`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee3f04cf566f6041aa9a0360494fd8db5ade383a) in **6.12.109**.
+
