+## Platform prerequisites, exact source and roles
+
+CephFS is registered with FS_USERNS_MOUNT. Current LXC namespace mapping retains namespace CAP_SYS_ADMIN, mount is not in the short seccomp denylist, and ceph/libceph are explicitly preloaded. A tenant administrator can mount a controlled Ceph cluster without an RBD device and feed the shared client decoder/placement code. The primary examples/scenarios explain cluster-peer control; formal AV:N/PR:N does not remove the prerequisite that a Ceph client session exists. Storage backup/NFS-server workload is not evidence of consuming a tenant-supplied Ceph cluster, so roles are node only.
+
