+## Platform prerequisites, exact source and roles
+
+NFS/NFS4 are registered with downstream FS_USERNS_MOUNT. Current LXC namespace mapping retains namespace CAP_SYS_ADMIN and the short seccomp denylist does not block mount or ordinary file activity. NFS client modules are explicitly preloaded. A tenant administrator can mount a controlled NFS server; no host block device is required. The exact NFS version, callbacks and teardown/failure sequence remain prerequisites. Storage hosts serve backup data over NFS; that server workload alone does not establish this client-side tenant mount trigger. Roles are therefore node only.
