+# CVE-2026-93817: perf address-filter lifetime use-after-free
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-93817.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 7.8 (HIGH), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+perf event addr_filter_ranges is read under RCU, but __free_event freed it immediately before readers had completed. Moving kfree to free_event_rcu preserves its lifetime through the grace period. The primary description is narrow and supplies no end-to-end exploit; downstream inherited-event/address-filter paths establish the relevant dangling-array read/copy lifetime.
+
+Mainline introduction: `4.7.0`, commit [`375637bc524952f1122ea22caf5a8f1fecad8228`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/375637bc524952f1122ea22caf5a8f1fecad8228). Mainline fixing commit: [`e62d4192e593630f355094adc467058a05bdc935`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e62d4192e593630f355094adc467058a05bdc935), first fixed final mainline release `7.2.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.111`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
