+# CVE-2026-97594: Landlock source-parent dentry use-after-free
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-97594.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 7.8 (HIGH), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+current_check_refer_path used old_dentry->d_parent without a reference or lock. linkat does not have the rename-path lock that protects hook_path_rename. Concurrent rename/rmdir can release that parent while Landlock walks its hierarchy. The fix uses dget/dget_parent and balances dput after checks and any synchronous audit. The primary KASAN report establishes a freed dentry read; arbitrary writes/control flow are not demonstrated by that report.
+
+Mainline introduction: `5.19.0`, commit [`b91c3e4ea756b12b7d992529226edce1cfd854d7`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b91c3e4ea756b12b7d992529226edce1cfd854d7). Mainline fixing commit: [`2c6dc792538260a8087ac5b22c31b3b8e47c85d6`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c6dc792538260a8087ac5b22c31b3b8e47c85d6), first fixed final mainline release `7.3.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.112`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
