+# CVE-2026-98039: BPF per-CPU kptr type confusion
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-98039.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The reviewed primary Linux CNA container supplies no CVSS score for this record; no score is invented. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+map_kptr_match_type allowed a plain allocated object or referenced kernel pointer in a BPF_KPTR_PERCPU field because the allowed-flags subset check did not require MEM_PERCPU. A later field load always adds MEM_PERCPU, so per-CPU pointer relocation and teardown interpret an ordinary pointer as a per-CPU allocation cookie. The primary fix explicitly identifies arbitrary kernel read/write for a plain allocation, with invalid relocation or missing-destructor paths for kernel pointers. The fix requires source MEM_PERCPU to match the destination field kind.
+
+Mainline introduction: `6.7.0`, commit [`36d8bdf75a93190e5669b9d1d95994e13e15ba1d`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36d8bdf75a93190e5669b9d1d95994e13e15ba1d). Mainline fixing commit: [`048029ba1c793f8cabc4ad5eea765da01903f8f1`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/048029ba1c793f8cabc4ad5eea765da01903f8f1), first fixed final mainline release `7.3.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.111`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
+| Branch | Affected from (inclusive) | Fixed from (exclusive affected bound) | Introduction commit | Fix commit |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 6.12 | 6.12.0 | 6.12.111 | [`36d8bdf75a93`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36d8bdf75a93190e5669b9d1d95994e13e15ba1d) | [`aaa9cf7707d1`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aaa9cf7707d1c5c0d2ca9d40c8b71652ac1c3c3f) |
+| 6.18 | 6.18.0 | 6.18.53 | [`36d8bdf75a93`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36d8bdf75a93190e5669b9d1d95994e13e15ba1d) | [`0bdd6121c8dd`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0bdd6121c8dd5f1764efe701ce26bb8e15acb172) |
+| 7.2 | 7.2.0 | 7.2.7 | [`36d8bdf75a93`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36d8bdf75a93190e5669b9d1d95994e13e15ba1d) | [`ad4ebae5dbc2`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad4ebae5dbc2d47b544aa54f03c12490065be08a) |
+
+Branches with direct CNA stable fixes and explicit older backport introductions are represented separately. Open EOL long-term branches inherit the original introduced code: after checking the CNA commit/CPE scope, no same-branch fix is asserted without a cited correction. Other short-lived branches use the stated global bounds; a custom source build needs an exact source identity rather than release-number inference. Makefile versions at individual fix commits precede the stable release bump and are used to identify branch, not to invent the first containing release.
+
+## Tenant reachability and configuration
+
+CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y in the archived build. The primitive needs a BTF kptr-capable map and program/kfunc access to the object allocation/per-CPU helpers; it is not established for a plain unprivileged socket-filter program. BTF loading requires bpf_token_capable(CAP_BPF), and eligible program types/kfunc sets, JIT and kernel BTF are further gates. Without deliberate valid token delegation, the relevant capability is initial-userns, not tenant userns. Current unprivileged_bpf_disabled=0 permits some BPF but does not confer these authorities. Actual delegated program/token/installed path remains unmeasured.
+
+The inspected current vpsAdmin feature/device code, vpsAdminOS container template and selected LXC profiles establish source behavior only. The template includes UID/GID mappings and the userns profile; capabilities retained there belong to the tenant user namespace. They do not satisfy an initial-user-namespace capability check. The default seccomp denylist blocks module loading and selected host interfaces, not arbitrary Linux syscalls; a per-container override remains a runtime fact.
+
+Necessary vulnerable-interface options declared for the shared collector:
+- `CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL`: archived .95 value `y`; requirement `enabled`.
+- `CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF`: archived .95 value `y`; requirement `enabled`.
+- `CONFIG_BPF_JIT`: archived .95 value `y`; requirement `enabled`.
+
+Archived exact .95 configuration SHA-256 is `c10922b492fdf39ed3027b9c8f7ce2846a5d3799d57d417a161595fa81a64969`, extracted from the frozen build NAR whose decompressed SHA-256 is `1b8ee65eed800b9ad10219936c50aa9b62fdae4f78ff9adcfaf2051eec40c229`. Producing vpsAdminOS revision is `c065fa2f8485399737e20e8ef9e44299d0766654`, Linux `a2384967b90f24d2470c9eb15f0e66d938df7e08`. This supports only that archived build, not every node or historical interval.
+
+Current downstream source check: The .113 map_kptr_match_type explicitly compares BPF_KPTR_PERCPU against the source MEM_PERCPU flag, matching aaa9cf77. No reviewed source default establishes token delegation to a VPS.
+
+The current site source inspected at `a2ad6da408715de811cc6d8ea7b29ac55ea341ec` uses [configs/node/base.nix](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsfree-cz-configuration/blob/a2ad6da408715de811cc6d8ea7b29ac55ea341ec/configs/node/base.nix) and [kernels.nix](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsfree-cz-configuration/blob/a2ad6da408715de811cc6d8ea7b29ac55ea341ec/configs/node/kernels.nix) for per-machine runtime kernel selection. The latter can consume an ignored local kernels.json; the reviewed tracked empty override maps therefore do not prove a deployed boot version. Exact source/dirty/closure identities from typed evidence remain necessary.
+
+## Roles, runtime and history
+
+Only the `node` role is applicable: the scoped attacker is a VPS process or delegated tenant VMM. Storage nodes run backups/NFS rather than VPSes; no matching storage-host trigger is established by this review. Kernel age alone does not expand that workload scope.
+
+The shared history baseline is `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z`. Node126 has a separately reviewed lifecycle override at `2026-03-31T20:11:46Z`; it is not copied from another dossier. No historical attestation is invented. Current booted configuration, ordered command line, effective sysctls, modules, source/closure identities and transition history must come from the one frozen shared typed-evidence collection. Current source defaults do not fill missing history. After this platform-wide reachability review, an affected historical release without the old configuration is conservatively affected; pre-introduction/fixed releases can classify without configuration. Custom builds require exact reviewed identities.
+
+Reviewed sysctl values: `{"kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled": ["0", "1", "2"]}`. Missing/unavailable/unreviewed values are unknown. Accepted values permit further evaluation; they do not encode an automatic mitigation. A host value does not prove tenant network-namespace state.
+
+Unmodeled prerequisites: program type,kfunc availability,token/capability delegation;not equivalent to ordinary socket-filter BPF. The evaluator has no generic module/device/CPU/LSM/program predicate. Any conservative result must be read with these limits; no unsupported YAML field or manual evaluation override is used.
+
+## Outcomes and protections
+
+The primary fix explicitly identifies an arbitrary kernel read/write primitive for the plain-allocation confusion, giving strong potential for node control when the privileged program prerequisites are met. This does not prove that ordinary VPS credentials can load that program or that a platform exploit was executed. VPS-root and cross-VPS effects are possible extensions; authority scope is central to the exposure conclusion.
+
+Allocator freelist hardening/randomization, allocation/free zeroing, stack initialization/protection, KASLR and FORTIFY in the archived build can raise exploit difficulty. They do not prove trigger prevention or repair this defect. Monitored warnings detect possible failed triggers and availability loss; monitoring is not prevention and does not show that production exploitation did not occur.
+
+## Mitigation and remaining evidence
+
+Upstream stable `6.12.111` contains the correction. No runtime livepatch/eBPF tuple is accepted merely from a historical coverage table. Exact patch content, source revision, module/version/boot kernel and clean OS identity plus activation/history must be reviewed before adding an accepted tuple. Empty accepted lists deliberately make no mitigation claim.
+
+The canonical [6.12.95 livepatch coverage page](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/docs/os/livepatches/6.12.95.md) was checked as historical coverage, not activation proof. No tuple or historical override from an older dossier is reused. The lead bilingual writing pass is complete. Evaluation uses the frozen shared snapshot described below; unresolved facts remain explicit. No collection, remote draft write, publication or email is performed by this source preparation.
+
