+# CVE-2026-98222: Encrypted-key datablob length overflow
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-98222.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The reviewed primary Linux CNA container supplies no CVSS score for this record; no score is invented. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+encrypted_key_alloc accumulated multiple string/data lengths into u16 datablob_len and key datalen, truncating the allocation length. __ekey_init then copied a long master-key description into the small payload; the primary KASAN report records a 32760-byte slab out-of-bounds write. The fix uses check_add_overflow for both 16-bit destinations and kzalloc_flex for the allocation.
+
+Mainline introduction: `2.6.38`, commit [`7e70cb4978507cf31d76b90e4cfb4c28cad87f0c`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7e70cb4978507cf31d76b90e4cfb4c28cad87f0c). Mainline fixing commit: [`8697c431e297eb0d0ab13dda6bc172b48a34f05c`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8697c431e297eb0d0ab13dda6bc172b48a34f05c), first fixed final mainline release `7.3.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.112`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
