+# CVE-2026-98260: POSIX CPU timer cleanup after failed exec
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-98260.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The primary Linux CNA container supplies CVSS 3.1, score 7.8 (HIGH), vector `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+A nonleader exec changes TID ownership in de_thread. A still-queued per-thread CPU timer can lose the PID lookup that would unlink it. A later exec failure after point_of_no_return reaches exit_itimers before posix_cpu_timers_exit, freeing a queued k_itimer; reaping then erases the freed rb-tree node. The fix moves POSIX timer cleanup immediately after de_thread, before later failure points.
+
+Mainline introduction: `5.7.0`, commit [`55e8c8eb2c7b6bf30e99423ccfe7ca032f498f59`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/55e8c8eb2c7b6bf30e99423ccfe7ca032f498f59). Mainline fixing commit: [`acb03d3881818581052924a9bbbe92b8741ed448`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/acb03d3881818581052924a9bbbe92b8741ed448), first fixed final mainline release `7.3.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.112`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
