+## Frozen evidence and reviewed lifecycle scope
+
+This dossier uses the single schema 8 snapshot collected at
+`2026-10-19T21:48:39Z`, SHA-256
+`61904e984266df2f6c53435b2b026b0d0980b35a23ed843eebf95b23c27c9274`.
+No per-CVE collection is performed. It contains 13 active nodes: 12 hypervisors
+report the fixed 6.12.113 source and one storage node lacks current/history
+security evidence. This is current-state evidence, not proof of earlier safety.
+The normal evaluator writes the tracked per-node conclusions; they are not
+edited manually.
+
+[Configuration commit e27882a9](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsfree-cz-configuration/commit/e27882a9bc8f6900903e6ae84841b9935190548c)
+first adds Node126 as a production hypervisor, including its node identity,
+module and cluster/netbootable registration. The independently reviewed parent
+`76055edbba3b3b4cf0cd6df45d2255e812d8aa6a` has neither that node nor its path.
+The frozen reconstructed history starts on the same day with booted release
+`6.12.70`, first observed at `2026-03-31T20:11:46Z`. Together these establish
+post-January lifecycle scope. The supported Node126-only history override starts
+at that retained baseline. The observation is not asserted as the exact
+production activation instant, and source/range/runtime classification still
+applies to every later interval. The global January 1 baseline is unchanged.
+There is no lifecycle override for storage161; missing evidence remains unknown
+when that role is applicable.
+
+Current runtime observations report `kernel.io_uring_disabled=0`,
+`kernel.io_uring_group=-1`, `kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled=0` and
+`kernel.perf_event_paranoid=2` on the 12 reporting hypervisors. Their exact collected
+configurations have `CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT=n`. These present facts do not reconstruct
+old config/LSM/program/device/CPU policy. The encrypted-key module is actually
+loaded on one reporting node, demonstrating why absence from a default preload
+list cannot establish fleet-wide non-exposure. Intel/AMD KVM vendor module
+observations do not by themselves prove nested VMX or IntelPT capabilities.
