+# CVE-2026-98586 — SCTP timer rearm before object reference acquisition
+
+Reviewed 2026-10-19. This dossier assesses the tenant-configured networking path; it is not a claim about every host service or every historical node configuration. The per-node evaluation is a separate evidence product.
+
+## Primary defect and evidence strength
+
+SCTP timer callbacks called mod_timer before acquiring the object reference for the new timer. Concurrent deletion can drop the reference and free the association/transport between these operations, after which the callback increments and later decrements a freed reference count. The correction takes the reference first and returns it if mod_timer reports an existing pending timer. It also covers the protocol-unreachable rearm path.
+
+The source establishes a refcount ordering race and stale-object refcount update. It does not supply a reliable attacker scheduling method or complete privilege-escalation chain.
+
+No formal CVSS metric is supplied in the reviewed Linux CNA container. The score and any CNA scenario assertions are source attribution, not a demonstrated vpsAdminOS escape or a substitute for the prerequisite analysis.
+
+## Introduction, stable fixes and exceptions
+
+The primary Linux CNA record places the global introduction at **2.6.12**, commit [`1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2), and the mainline fix at **7.3.0**, commit [`cae23ae3f7887a1cf8a75da38edcebeef695040f`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=cae23ae3f7887a1cf8a75da38edcebeef695040f). The 6.12 correction is [`27c51a9b55b227309161c903f9ecfbf022516bc2`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27c51a9b55b227309161c903f9ecfbf022516bc2) in **6.12.112**.
+
