+# CVE-2026-98720: KVM enlightened nested TPR isolation bypass
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-98720.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The reviewed primary Linux CNA container supplies no CVSS score for this record; no score is invented. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+Changing runtime enlightened-VMCS controls did not force refresh of the nested MSR bitmap. Switching TPR virtualization off after L2 had run with it on could retain TPR passthrough, allowing L2 or L1 by proxy to read/write L0 TPR. The fix sets force_msr_bitmap_recalc when runtime control groups are dirty. Access to the host task-priority register is an explicit L0 boundary violation, not proof of arbitrary host memory/root control.
+
+Mainline introduction: `5.17.0`, commit [`502d2bf5f2fd7c05adc2d4f057910bd5d4c4c63e`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/502d2bf5f2fd7c05adc2d4f057910bd5d4c4c63e). Mainline fixing commit: [`2abb25273c82061dd4670690c81c319c03740bf6`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2abb25273c82061dd4670690c81c319c03740bf6), first fixed final mainline release `7.3.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.113`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
+
+| Branch | Affected from (inclusive) | Fixed from (exclusive affected bound) | Introduction commit | Fix commit |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 6.1 | 6.1.0 | Open: no same-branch fix in reviewed CNA references | [`502d2bf5f2fd`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/502d2bf5f2fd7c05adc2d4f057910bd5d4c4c63e) | — |
+| 6.6 | 6.6.0 | Open: no same-branch fix in reviewed CNA references | [`502d2bf5f2fd`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/502d2bf5f2fd7c05adc2d4f057910bd5d4c4c63e) | — |
+| 6.12 | 6.12.0 | 6.12.113 | [`502d2bf5f2fd`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/502d2bf5f2fd7c05adc2d4f057910bd5d4c4c63e) | [`2db11598b59f`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2db11598b59f16ddb6420693f9a4ac4efc3d4789) |
+| 6.18 | 6.18.0 | 6.18.56 | [`502d2bf5f2fd`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/502d2bf5f2fd7c05adc2d4f057910bd5d4c4c63e) | [`f6189e26d023`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6189e26d0237e47e2f04f9cb1e43fd19a9b2f3a) |
+| 7.2 | 7.2.0 | 7.2.10 | [`502d2bf5f2fd`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/502d2bf5f2fd7c05adc2d4f057910bd5d4c4c63e) | [`1e497e3bdab6`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1e497e3bdab6983deb68a1d26b488027deb4527f) |
+
+Branches with direct CNA stable fixes and explicit older backport introductions are represented separately. Open EOL long-term branches inherit the original introduced code: after checking the CNA commit/CPE scope, no same-branch fix is asserted without a cited correction. Other short-lived branches use the stated global bounds; a custom source build needs an exact source identity rather than release-number inference. Makefile versions at individual fix commits precede the stable release bump and are used to identify branch, not to invent the first containing release.
+
+## Tenant reachability and configuration
+
+KVM/KVM_INTEL=m and KVM_HYPERV=y in the exact archived build. A delegated tenant VMM can enable KVM_CAP_HYPERV_ENLIGHTENED_VMCS through ordinary KVM_ENABLE_CAP when supported; this is guest eVMCS support, distinct from host-under-Hyper-V enlightened acceleration. Intel VMX/nested/eVMCS availability, relevant enlightened MSR bitmap feature and TPR control sequence remain runtime/guest prerequisites. Device policy and source nested defaults are not observed hardware proof.
+
+The inspected current vpsAdmin feature/device code, vpsAdminOS container template and selected LXC profiles establish source behavior only. The template includes UID/GID mappings and the userns profile; capabilities retained there belong to the tenant user namespace. They do not satisfy an initial-user-namespace capability check. The default seccomp denylist blocks module loading and selected host interfaces, not arbitrary Linux syscalls; a per-container override remains a runtime fact.
+
+Necessary vulnerable-interface options declared for the shared collector:
+- `CONFIG_KVM`: archived .95 value `m`; requirement `enabled`.
+- `CONFIG_KVM_INTEL`: archived .95 value `m`; requirement `enabled`.
+- `CONFIG_KVM_HYPERV`: archived .95 value `y`; requirement `enabled`.
+
+Archived exact .95 configuration SHA-256 is `c10922b492fdf39ed3027b9c8f7ce2846a5d3799d57d417a161595fa81a64969`, extracted from the frozen build NAR whose decompressed SHA-256 is `1b8ee65eed800b9ad10219936c50aa9b62fdae4f78ff9adcfaf2051eec40c229`. Producing vpsAdminOS revision is `c065fa2f8485399737e20e8ef9e44299d0766654`, Linux `a2384967b90f24d2470c9eb15f0e66d938df7e08`. This supports only that archived build, not every node or historical interval.
+
+Current downstream source check: The .113 copy_enlightened_to_vmcs12 tests runtime control clean bits and forces MSR-bitmap recalculation, matching 2db11598. The code preserves the difference between guest eVMCS capability and host Hyper-V environment.
+
+The current site source inspected at `a2ad6da408715de811cc6d8ea7b29ac55ea341ec` uses [configs/node/base.nix](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsfree-cz-configuration/blob/a2ad6da408715de811cc6d8ea7b29ac55ea341ec/configs/node/base.nix) and [kernels.nix](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsfree-cz-configuration/blob/a2ad6da408715de811cc6d8ea7b29ac55ea341ec/configs/node/kernels.nix) for per-machine runtime kernel selection. The latter can consume an ignored local kernels.json; the reviewed tracked empty override maps therefore do not prove a deployed boot version. Exact source/dirty/closure identities from typed evidence remain necessary.
+
+## Roles, runtime and history
+
+Only the `node` role is applicable: the scoped attacker is a VPS process or delegated tenant VMM. Storage nodes run backups/NFS rather than VPSes; no matching storage-host trigger is established by this review. Kernel age alone does not expand that workload scope.
+
+The shared history baseline is `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z`. Node126 has a separately reviewed lifecycle override at `2026-03-31T20:11:46Z`; it is not copied from another dossier. No historical attestation is invented. Current booted configuration, ordered command line, effective sysctls, modules, source/closure identities and transition history must come from the one frozen shared typed-evidence collection. Current source defaults do not fill missing history. After this platform-wide reachability review, an affected historical release without the old configuration is conservatively affected; pre-introduction/fixed releases can classify without configuration. Custom builds require exact reviewed identities.
+
+Unmodeled prerequisites: Intel VMX/nested/eVMCS exposure;actual module/device. The evaluator has no generic module/device/CPU/LSM/program predicate. Any conservative result must be read with these limits; no unsupported YAML field or manual evaluation override is used.
+
+## Outcomes and protections
+
+The primary report explicitly establishes L0 TPR read/write through the faulty nested controls. Node availability is plausible from host interrupt-priority effects. Arbitrary node-root/kernel-code execution and cross-VPS access are possible extensions, not demonstrated by this register-level primitive; VPS-root escalation is not the direct mechanism.
+
+Allocator freelist hardening/randomization, allocation/free zeroing, stack initialization/protection, KASLR and FORTIFY in the archived build do not address the demonstrated direct access to L0's task-priority register. The reviewed source and reports establish no dependent exploitation step for which those settings provide relevant protection. Correct MSR-bitmap refresh repairs the defect; Intel VMX and enlightened nested-virtualization prerequisites still limit its reachability. Monitored warnings detect possible failed triggers and availability loss; monitoring is not prevention and does not show that production exploitation did not occur.
+
+## Mitigation and remaining evidence
+
+Upstream stable `6.12.113` contains the correction. No runtime livepatch/eBPF tuple is accepted merely from a historical coverage table. Exact patch content, source revision, module/version/boot kernel and clean OS identity plus activation/history must be reviewed before adding an accepted tuple. Empty accepted lists deliberately make no mitigation claim.
+
+The canonical [6.12.95 livepatch coverage page](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/vpsadminos/blob/87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088/docs/os/livepatches/6.12.95.md) was checked as historical coverage, not activation proof. No tuple or historical override from an older dossier is reused. The lead bilingual writing pass is complete. Evaluation uses the frozen shared snapshot described below; unresolved facts remain explicit. No collection, remote draft write, publication or email is performed by this source preparation.
+
+## Source references
