+# CVE-2026-98858: io_uring SQPOLL task-work use-after-free
+
+## Decision and source scope
+
+Approved member-relevance assessment; unpublished draft candidate. [Primary Linux CNA record](https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/security/vulns/+/56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9/cve/published/2026/CVE-2026-98858.json) is PUBLISHED at snapshot `56fdb3bed3f95b64b83c9f1a42ccb603452ec5c9`, reviewed on 2026-10-19. This assessment does not claim production exploitation or a completed platform exploit test. The authenticated preflight found no existing CVE/external-ID or local dossier duplicate in its 56-advisory/57-CVE scope.
+
+## Formal severity
+
+The reviewed primary Linux CNA container supplies no CVSS score for this record; no score is invented. These formal source scores are separate from the platform outcomes below. The snapshot has no per-record update timestamp; its exact source revision and review date bind this assessment.
+
+## Defect and correction
+
+Publishing the final request to the SQPOLL task-work list can let the polling thread complete it and free ctx/tctx before io_req_normal_work_add finishes using them. The primary report contains both a four-byte freed-object read and an eight-byte freed-object write. The fix holds an RCU read section across publication and waits for a grace period for SQPOLL ring destruction.
+
+Mainline introduction: `6.9.0`, commit [`af5d68f8892f8ee8f137648b79ceb2abc153a19b`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af5d68f8892f8ee8f137648b79ceb2abc153a19b). Mainline fixing commit: [`a92193c91e8839fe5fc209616ea95465ae4b919d`](https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a92193c91e8839fe5fc209616ea95465ae4b919d), first fixed final mainline release `7.3.0`. Stable first correction in the requested inclusive range: `6.12.113`. The CNA Git intervals, semantic versions and CPE applicability were checked together; this is not a CVE-number/date cutoff.
